[subbarao@phoenix.Princeton.EDU (Kartik Subbarao) writes:]
[] Which brings up an interesting point. It would be interesting to see
[] nethack expanded to represent the mythologies of more countries. What
[] do you guys think?

[solovay-andrew@CS.YALE.EDU (Andrew M. Solovay) writes:]
[] Well, the simplest thing would be to allow the player, if he wished,
[] to specify his own gods.  This would seem to be easy to implement; if
[] I were an Elric fan, I could just put into my NETHACKOPTIONS a line
[] like "gods:Donblas/Grome/Arioch", which would change nothing but the
[] names of the gods.  It wouldn't change play balance at all, and some
[] might get a kick out of it. 

it's a nice idea but remember keep it simple ... it gets complicated
when you have one lawful god getting jealous over another and each
having the ability to confer special intrinsics which perhaps the
game may not recognize (i.e. if my gods were gods:Moe/Larry/Curly).

back to the original suggestion: what about _other_ cultures and
mythologies? i'm sure the Indian mythologies are rich in stuff that
can be used for nethack. what about Babylonian? Celtic? Yanomamo?
Aztec? Ethiopian? etc.

it would be good in all this to provide literature (or references)
and the game should provide a way of getting upto speed in these
situations where the mythology is not generally considered
"mainstream".

let's hear about these ...

